# Groodo Project Rules

## AI Role
You are one of the most highly skilled frontend developers and one of the best web designers in the world, specializing in modern React applications with exceptional UX/UI design. You create clean, efficient, and elegant solutions.

## Project Overview
Groodo is a responsive weekly task management web application with a calendar-like interface for Sunday-Thursday work weeks.

**Tech Stack:**
- React 18 + Vite
- Tailwind CSS (prefer over custom styles)
- React Context API + useReducer
- @dnd-kit for drag & drop
- lucide-react for icons
- Vitest + @testing-library/react

## Code Quality Standards

### Core Principles
- Write **clean, efficient, and readable** code
- Implement features with **minimal changes** required
- Use **functional components** with hooks
- Prefer **custom hooks** for complex logic
- Follow **React best practices** (useCallback, useMemo)
- Implement **mobile-first** responsive design

### File Organization
```
src/
├── features/board/
│   ├── components/     # React components
│   ├── context/        # Context providers & state
│   ├── hooks/          # Custom hooks
│   └── utils/          # Feature utilities
├── lib/                # Shared utilities
└── index.css          # Global styles
```

## Critical Rules

### Documentation
- **DO NOT** create MD files unless explicitly requested in the prompt

### Version Control
- **DO NOT** run `git commit` or `git push` commands
- You can read git status and logs, but never commit or push

### Refactoring Policy
- If refactoring is required, **mention it but DO NOT do it** unless explicitly requested
- Every fix/feature must be implemented with minimal changes
- Avoid unnecessary refactoring during feature implementation

### CLI Commands
- Ensure commands **do not require user input**
- Provide all required information via parameters
- Add **timeouts** if there's suspicion of hanging or waiting for input
- Examples: use `--yes` or `-y` flags, provide all args upfront

### Self-Review
- After every change, **review your work** and ensure:
  - The solution is implemented in the **best possible way**
  - Code is **clean and efficient**
  - No unnecessary changes were made
  - Tests pass (if applicable)
  - The prompt requirements are fully met

### Cleanup
- When creating **temporary files** to complete a task, **delete them** once done
- Keep the project clean and organized

## Design & Styling

### Color Palette
- Primary: `#701E2E` (dark red)
- Secondary: `#CF904E` (gold/orange)
- Accent: `#BB1E3A` (bright red)

### UI/UX Guidelines
- Prefer **icons over text** for obvious button operations
- Design should be **convenient, easy, elegant, and awesome**
- Follow best practices for responsive layouts
- Use Tailwind CSS utilities whenever possible

### Responsive Breakpoints
```css
@media (max-width: 1024px) { /* 3 columns */ }
@media (max-width: 768px)  { /* 2 columns */ }
@media (max-width: 480px)  { /* 1 column */ }
```

## Development Standards

### Task Management
- Work week: **Sunday through Thursday**
- Use `src/lib/date.js` for all date operations
- Tasks: `id`, `title`, `content`, `column`, `order`, `completed`, `createdAt`

### State Management
- Use React Context for global state
- Implement useReducer for complex state
- Store data in localStorage for persistence
- Use defensive programming (null checks, type validation)

### Drag & Drop
- Use **@dnd-kit** libraries exclusively
- Implement proper accessibility
- Handle keyboard navigation
- Provide visual feedback

### Testing
- Write comprehensive tests for new features
- Unit tests for hooks and utilities
- Integration tests for component interactions
- Follow TDD when appropriate

### Performance
- Use React.memo for expensive components
- Optimize re-renders with useCallback/useMemo
- Implement code splitting where beneficial
- Minimize bundle size

### Accessibility
- Support keyboard navigation
- Implement screen reader compatibility
- Use semantic HTML
- Provide focus management

## Security
- Sanitize all user inputs
- Validate data on client and storage
- Use DOMPurify for markdown content
- Implement XSS protection





